{"id": "EUVD-2026-86715", "enisaUuid": "df65f0a5-c109-3cbc-bd1b-3f6244d71a1c", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Mark signal tracepoint siginfo arguments as scalar\n\nThe signal_generate and signal_deliver tracepoints declare their info\nargument as a struct kernel_siginfo pointer. btf_ctx_access() therefore\ntreats it as a trusted pointer for tp_btf programs.\n\nSignal delivery also uses SEND_SIG_NOINFO and SEND_SIG_PRIV as special\nvalues for this argument. Those values are zero and one respectively,\nand are not pointers. A tp_btf program can currently dereference either\nvalue and fault the kernel. In particular, signal_generate can run from\ntimer interrupt context, turning the fault into a kernel panic.\n\nRecord both tracepoints in raw_tp_null_args[] and mark argument one as\na non-pointer. This preserves scalar access to the cookie while rejecting\ndirect and helper-mediated pointer use. Merely marking it nullable would\nnot suffice because SEND_SIG_PRIV is nonzero.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:24:06", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:54:20", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/05757377fa0447163d07c43a119f81abe1eef8dc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0e78cb242a57e481061fcb542fed4d51afba25c4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d2eaea3599bcce659ce91862254dc91bcbdb6351", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/77515ab12e4983e6416f8c35039a3f0c0822ac70"], "aliases": ["GHSA-x678-33cq-r6hr", "CVE-2026-98062"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.12, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "175921cc-16ec-3a77-ad9c-0808087fdcf6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "838a10bd2ebfe11a60dd67687533a7cfc220cc86 <77515ab12e4983e6416f8c35039a3f0c0822ac70"}, {"id": "3902bafd-5f14-3ab9-a9a3-fac7d469fa5f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "65307e84-6207-32a9-84ed-ab557b077210", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "838a10bd2ebfe11a60dd67687533a7cfc220cc86 <0e78cb242a57e481061fcb542fed4d51afba25c4"}, {"id": "98a3d45f-4185-3448-8f48-fe97ec3ddecd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "aea4f512-4c22-3fbd-b075-f5ff58231641", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "c2611c7c-88be-39b7-8521-d403a364d2c8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.13"}, {"id": "d9b91c79-735a-3d9a-a375-1d6b86329a1d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "e3be1b00-d5d9-394b-af56-5f4823064474", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "ea177b11-f6db-3a27-b5a0-091f936ae295", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.12.6 <6.12.114"}, {"id": "ecc7d26b-694b-3d9c-8197-80f99650c6f4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "838a10bd2ebfe11a60dd67687533a7cfc220cc86 <d2eaea3599bcce659ce91862254dc91bcbdb6351"}, {"id": "efe6d3a8-58c1-36c0-a192-897e604d1d7e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b2fc4b17fc13810ef440fb323fad3981cd174985 <05757377fa0447163d07c43a119f81abe1eef8dc"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "afed4cdf-bdb5-3d15-b74c-b56667cbe41c", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}